 "notes": [
  "Source: embedded raster image xref 269 (DeviceGray 1506x723 px, 300 ppi) on PDF page 13, extracted with doc.extract_image; placed at bbox (117.02, 295.97, 478.46, 469.49) pt.",
  "Calibration per panel: axes spines (x: beta=15 and 90 deg; y: Gamma=0 and 5) located as darkness-weighted centroids, plus gray gridlines at beta=30,45,60,75 and Gamma=1..4; linear least-squares fit, max residual 0.25 px (x) and 0.42 px (y). Scale: 5.395 px/deg, 87.63 px per unit Gamma (1 px = 0.0114 Gamma).",
  "Curve separation: pixels darker than 128 inside the axes (label boxes masked). The solid line is the single large connected component and is always the lowest run in a column / leftmost run in a row; dashes are the separate small components. In panel alpha=1 the last dashes (beta>83.8) touch the solid line: there the solid centre was taken from the bottom edge and the dashed centre from the top edge (minus/plus half the local run height).",
  "Centre-line points: column scans where the line is shallow (run height < 2 line widths) and row scans where it is steep; dash ends (5 px) excluded. Line width ~7.0 px.",
  "Values reported are from a piecewise-linear least-squares fit (perpendicular distance, soft-L1) with knots every 5 deg (15,20,...,90). The plotted curves are evidently polylines through data at 5-deg steps: fit RMS 0.12-0.24 px for all 6 curves; 2.5-deg knots do not improve the fit materially, 10-deg knots fail (RMS 3-13 px). Hence the values at beta=15,20,...,90 are the vertices of the plotted polylines.",
  "Sensitivity of the knot values to the darkness threshold (96/128/160) and to the dash-end margin (3/5/8 px): <= 0.002 for in-axis knots except beta=90 (<= 0.004).",
  "Reading uncertainty (per point in 'uncertainty'): +-0.01 Gamma (about 1 px) typically; +-0.02 for the first in-axis vertex just below the top of the axis (steep kink), for beta=90 (extrapolated about 1 deg under the right spine) and for the alpha=1 dashed curve at 85-90 deg (merged with solid line); +-0.03 for the alpha=10 dashed value at 90 deg (only a short final dash 86-89 deg).",
  "null = curve above the top of the axis (Gamma > 5) or no curve (beta=15, 20). The 'implied_offaxis_knots' are extrapolations of the first visible segment to the previous 5-deg knot (assuming the 5-deg polyline model); they are NOT read from the figure and are rough. alpha=10 dashed at 30 deg is not given (only 14% of that segment visible).",
  "'beta_where_curve_crosses_top_Gamma5' is where the fitted polyline leaves the top of the axis (for alpha=10 dashed it is read from the small top dash piece, ~34.4 deg, +-0.3).",
  "'direct_column_readings_crosscheck' are model-free local readings at the knot columns (local linear fit to centre-line points within +-2.5 px, null in dash gaps); they agree with the polyline vertices within 0.00-0.03 except at sharp kinks near the top (alpha=1 solid 25 deg: 3.425 vs 3.374) where the local fit straddles the kink and is biased.",
  "Ordering check: for every beta and alpha the dashed (K.v'_opt) curve is above the solid (-grad u'_FE) one, and both increase with alpha, consistent with the paper's text."
 ],
